        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Rootborn</strong> is a quirky action-platformer—basically, a sandbox adventure.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It’s like the lovechild of <strong>Terraria</strong> and schizophrenia. Brother to <strong>Starbound</strong> and the dirt on your sneakers, inspired by squares.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Imagine mixing weird art style, a random story, four cans of booze, and a unhealthy obsession with stacking game blocks. That’s what you get.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Game that scares clowns, spiders, and heights (probably).<br>(Okay, maybe not completely, but you get the idea.)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Game that took 17,000 years and 96 trillions of neurons to make this game.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Game that cost about the same as 3 slices of pizzas and a free water cup.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Game that is the reason its developer is now unemployed and lonely.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Meet <strong>Rootborn</strong>.</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Rootborn</strong> is a quirky action-platformer—basically, a sandbox adventure.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It’s like the lovechild of <strong>Terraria</strong> and schizophrenia. Brother to <strong>Starbound</strong> and the dirt on your sneakers, inspired by squares.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Imagine mixing weird art style, a random story, four cans of booze, and a unhealthy obsession with stacking game blocks. That’s what you get.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Game that scares clowns, spiders, and heights (probably).<br>(Okay, maybe not completely, but you get the idea.)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Game that took 17,000 years and 96 trillions of neurons to make this game.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Game that cost about the same as 3 slices of pizzas and a free water cup.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Game that is the reason its developer is now unemployed and lonely.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Meet <strong>Rootborn</strong>.</p>",
        "short_description": "A cozy action-platformer with an open world that, of course, 99% of players will pirate. And in the end, all the nonlinear story, filled with battles, building, entertainment, and much more... the developer did it all for free.",
